.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-update - Change a payment's description


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the description of a payment — the one field that can be edited after
create. Either party (payer or payee) may do it, in any status, closed ones
included.

.PP
The description lives only on the gateway: it is in nothing signed or hashed
on-chain, so this moves no money, needs no signing key and sends no webhook.
At most 255 characters.

.PP
Pass the new text with --description, or --clear to remove it (exactly one).

.PP
Requires login — run 'rail0 auth login -p 0xKey…' first.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--clear\fP[=false]
	Remove the description

.PP
\fB-d\fP, \fB--description\fP=""
	New description (max 255 characters)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments update 0xabc123… -d "order #42"
  rail0 payments update 0xabc123… --clear
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
